WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.110
(audience cheering)
- We are back

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:03.270
and you have seen it
happen from time to time.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.670
Here on this show, I get
to talking with guests

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.760
and the conversations go along
'cause mama likes to talk.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.770
That's why we keep a vault of interviews

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.360
we couldn't fit in the original show,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.790
but we want to make sure
that you don't miss.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.847
Today's Kelly Extra takes
us back to September

00:00:16.847 --> 00:00:19.200
when we had Scarlett Johansson here.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.330
We got to talking about our kids and one

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.910
of the cardinal Marvel Universe rules

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.500
she said she would never break.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:26.700
Check it out.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.380
When Jeremy Renner was
here, he was talking

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:31.320
about how he used his Hawkeye
costume for Halloween.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:33.060
Have you ever done that?
- What?

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.200
- You never done that?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.090
I would totally do that.
- That's allowed?

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.887
Marvel never told me I could do that.

00:00:37.887 --> 00:00:40.590
- I don't, I feel like Jeremy maybe says,

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:41.910
sorry doesn't ask permission.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.116
- Yeah.
- Maybe he's

00:00:43.116 --> 00:00:43.950
one of those people.
- You're actually right.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:44.940
That's definitely...
- I'm one of those people.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.853
So yeah, 'cause then you
can always say sorry later.

00:00:47.853 --> 00:00:48.884
- I get it.
- I would totally do it.

00:00:48.884 --> 00:00:49.727
- I'm not, I am very by the books.

00:00:49.727 --> 00:00:52.830
I don't, I am the person that is,

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.440
I don't wanna be, I'm constantly,

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.390
I worked for Marvel for 10 years

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.580
and I was constantly
terrified I was going to

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.343
spoil some major-
- spoil something?

00:01:01.343 --> 00:01:03.306
- anything from the color of my,

00:01:03.306 --> 00:01:06.390
that it's like now a darker shade of Navy

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.767
it was like, you can't say a thing.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.850
- Oh, wow.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.300
I'm sort of programmed to never-

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.738
- Sounds a little abusive, but yeah,

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:15.420
you're programmed. (laughs)

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.851
- Sorry

00:01:16.851 --> 00:01:17.684
please. Yeah

00:01:17.684 --> 00:01:18.900
- I would, I don't do well with secrets

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.310
or anything like that
so I would hate that.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.300
Having to keep a secret.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.133
I don't know.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.390
- There was definitely
cast members like, you know

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:25.223
- That are like me?

00:01:25.223 --> 00:01:27.460
Yeah. That are really, really bad at it

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:29.400
that are like a liability.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.510
- I call it passion.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:31.350
We're just excited

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.870
about something so that's why
we give it away an accident.

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:34.890
But the, you said 10 years

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:36.904
and this is like the 10th anniversary of

00:01:36.904 --> 00:01:37.737
the first Marvel movie coming out.

00:01:37.737 --> 00:01:38.760
So like or Avengers movie coming out.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.080
So what do you remember

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.063
like what's one of your favorite ones?

00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:42.511
Like, of being a part of it?

00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:43.680
- I mean, because

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:45.180
- It seems like such a fun set.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:46.380
- It's, they're all, yeah.

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.950
I've had the most fun on
the, on the Marvel movies.

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:51.210
Just 'cuz you have a whole family

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.950
there that you come back to.

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:53.783
- Yeah.

00:01:53.783 --> 00:01:55.590
- Every, you know, year
and a half or whatever.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.334
And so, you know, it's been
an adjustment not having

00:01:59.334 --> 00:02:01.420
you know, my, my peeps around like that.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.590
Yeah. I would say, you
know, the first Avengers was

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.322
amazing just because it was
such a, you felt it was just

00:02:07.322 --> 00:02:08.520
like Wild West

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:13.470
and not that genre had not
been, you know, it was, it was

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.533
- Not just quite established

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:15.366
- Quite established like that.

00:02:15.366 --> 00:02:16.890
Yeah. It wasn't established
exactly in the same way.

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.140
And so it felt like we were doing some

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.480
we didn't know if it was
gonna work and you know

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.313
just kind of felt like a crazy thing.

00:02:22.313 --> 00:02:24.383
It worked, turn out

00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:26.221
- It worked for all the crazies
like me, like I am obsessed.

00:02:26.221 --> 00:02:27.273
I love them.

